From cbe63a8358310244e6007398bd2c7c70c7fd51cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Vok=C3=A1=C4=8D?= <michal.vokac@ysoft.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Mar 2020 09:46:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: imx6dl-yapp4: Fix Ursa board Ethernet connection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Y Soft yapp4 platform supports up to two Ethernet ports.
The Ursa board though has only one Ethernet port populated and that is
the port@2. Since the introduction of this platform into mainline a wrong
port was deleted and the Ethernet could never work. Fix this by deleting
the correct port node.

Fixes: 87489ec3a77f ("ARM: dts: imx: Add Y Soft IOTA Draco, Hydra and Ursa boards")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Michal Vokáč <michal.vokac@ysoft.com>
Signed-off-by: Shawn Guo <shawnguo@kernel.org>

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6dl-yapp4-ursa.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6dl-yapp4-ursa.dts
index 0d594e4bd559..a1173bf5bff5 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6dl-yapp4-ursa.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6dl-yapp4-ursa.dts
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@ &reg_usb_h1_vbus {
 };

 &switch_ports {
-	/delete-node/ port@2;
+	/delete-node/ port@3;
 };

 &touchscreen {
-- 
2.25.1

You are a programming expert.

You will be given the root cause of a bug.

Based on these details, your task is to determine whether the provided code snippet contains the bug.
Think step by step.
Be conservative in your assessment. If you are unsure, answer "no."

Root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect deletion of the Ethernet port node in the device tree source file for the Ursa board. Specifically, the deletion of `port@2` instead of `port@3` led to the non-functionality of the Ethernet connection, as the Ursa board only has one Ethernet port, which is `port@2`. This misconfiguration prevented the Ethernet from working properly since the necessary port node was removed.



Now, determine whether the provided code snippet is buggy:

&switch_ports {
	/delete-node/ port@2;
};

&touchscreen {
	status = "okay";


